    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Пожалуйста, поговори с папой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Please talk to dad.' Here 'talk' sets up the idea, while 'dad' comes at the end for emphasis. And Nastya jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Я постараюсь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will try.' Notice the word order: 'I' comes first, and 'to try' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А что это такое?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And what is this?' The first content word means 'what', and 'on earth' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "valya",
      "t": "Это мой десерт.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is my dessert.' You'll hear 'this' all the time in the show, here connected with 'dessert'. Max answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Прямо как у шефа.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Just like the Chef's.' Here 'right' sets up the idea, while 'chef' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "valya",
      "t": "Спасибо большое.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Thank you very much.' the speaker starts with 'thank you' and pairs it with 'big' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Можно попробовать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Can I taste it?' Max puts 'may' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'to taste'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "valya",
      "t": "Конечно, бери.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Of course, take it.' the speaker starts with 'of course' and pairs it with 'take' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это очень вкусно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is very tasty.' The first content word means 'this', and 'it's tasty' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Да, мне тоже нравится.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, I like it too.' A compact expression built around 'to me' and 'is pleasing'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "valya",
      "t": "Я долго учился этому.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I studied this for a long time.' the speaker puts 'I' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'for a long time'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты молодец, Валя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well done, Valya.' Listen for the word meaning 'you' right alongside 'well done' in this line.",
